  "published": "2026-11-15T20:01:23.94Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Release 2.0.0:\n- Major Architecture: Introduced object-oriented Document class (new Document(), LoadFromFile(), LoadFromBytes(), LoadFromString(), LoadFromStream(), ConvertToPdf()).\n- Namespace Redesign: Moved DocumentFormat and introduced concise Format enum directly in root Efizzy namespace.\n- Global Usings: Added automatic MSBuild build and buildTransitive props providing zero-effort global usings for consumer projects.\n- Deprecation: Deprecated legacy string-based format overloads on Doc2PdfConverter in favor of strongly-typed Format enums.\n- Performance: Retained zero-copy in-process execution, streaming architecture, and instant sub-5ms conversions.\n\nRelease 1.1.1:\n- Performance & Size: Decoupled desktop engine dependencies and enabled Link-Time Optimization (LTO) dead code elimination, reducing native binary footprint by ~16%.\n- Native Engine: Introduced modular dynamic loader for native rendering components.\n\nRelease 1.1.0:\n- Feature: Automatic format resolution via magic byte inspection (DocumentFormat.Auto).\n- Security: Zero-trust defense intercepting disguised executables (PE, ELF, Mach-O, LNK, scripts, CHM).\n- Security: Path traversal protection, null-byte sanitization, and cryptographic unmanaged password zeroing.\n- Performance: Zero-allocation cached format pointers, zero-allocation ASCII sniffing, and zero-copy MemoryStream conversions.\n- Engine: Streamlined native CSS preprocessor and standards-compliant HTML5 DOCTYPE handling.",
